## Why This Is Asked
This probes ability to design extensible, runtime-configurable pipelines that manage cross‑cutting concerns without redeploys, a common need in large SaaS platforms.

## Key Concepts
- Runtime extensibility
- Middleware pipeline composition
- Async control flow and short-circuiting
- Registry pattern with per-route overrides

## Code Example
```typescript
interface Request { /* ... */ }
interface Response { /* ... */ }
type Next = (continueChain?: boolean) => Promise<void>;
type MiddlewareFactory = () => Middleware;
interface Middleware {
  handle(req: Request, res: Response, next: Next): Promise<void>;
}
class Registry {
  private map = new Map<string, MiddlewareFactory>();
  register(name: string, factory: MiddlewareFactory) { this.map.set(name, factory); }
  create(name: string): Middleware | null { const f = this.map.get(name); return f ? f() : null; }
}
class RoutePipeline {
  constructor(private registry: Registry, private routeMiddlewares: string[]) {}
  async handle(req: Request, res: Response) {
    let i = 0;
    const next: Next = async (continueChain = true) => {
      if (!continueChain || i >= this.routeMiddlewares.length) return;
      const mwName = this.routeMiddlewares[i++];
      const mw = this.registry.create(mwName);
      if (mw) await mw.handle(req, res, next);
    };
    await next();
  }
}
```

## Follow-up Questions
- How to test, mock, and snapshot middleware behavior in isolation?
- How to handle errors within middleware and propagate to a centralized logger?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests understanding of the Command pattern, runtime extensibility, and error isolation in interactive tools. It’s practical for editors, CLIs, or worker pipelines that want to grow without touching core runtimes.

## Key Concepts

- Command interface with execute/undo
- Runtime registry for plugin-like commands
- Per-command state needed for accurate undo
- Isolation: boundaries catch/handle command failures
- Undo/redo stack management

## Code Example

```javascript
interface Command {
  execute(): void;
  undo(): void;
}
class Registry {
  private factories = new Map<string, () => Command>();
  register(name: string, factory: () => Command) {
    this.factories.set(name, factory);
  }
  create(name: string): Command {
    const f = this.factories.get(name);
    if (!f) throw new Error(`Unknown command: ${name}`);
    return f();
  }
}
class EditorState {
  content: string = "";
}
class InsertText implements Command {
  constructor(private state: EditorState, private pos: number, private text: string) {}
  private prev: string = "";
  execute() {
    this.prev = this.state.content;
    this.state.content =
      this.state.content.slice(0, this.pos) + this.text + this.state.content.slice(this.pos);
  }
  undo() {
    this.state.content = this.prev;
  }
}
```

